<Layout title="Offshore staffing for Australian businesses" description="Add dedicated offshore capacity to your Australian business. Scope skills, state-specific working hours and support with iHire Global." crumbs={[{name:'Australian offshore staffing',url:'/au/offshore-staffing/'}]}><PageHero title="More capacity for a business that keeps moving." intro="Add dedicated offshore employees to your Australian team without running the recruitment and employment infrastructure yourself. You lead the work; iHire supports the hire."/><section class="section wrap compact-top detail-grid"><div><h2>Match coverage to your customers.</h2><p>An Australian business may serve customers across several time zones. Define which local hours matter for the role, the state or territory your team operates in, and how daylight saving affects handovers.</p><p>Customer service, sales support and e-commerce administration can all benefit from an agreed coverage window. After-hours work requires explicit shifts, escalation procedures and infrastructure planning.</p><h2>Keep ownership with your team.</h2><p>A dedicated employee works within your operating procedures and approval processes. Your manager sets priorities, provides training and reviews performance, while iHire manages the employment administration.</p><a class="text-link" href="/how-it-works/">See how hiring works →</a></div><aside class="surface-panel"><h2>Confirm the details around your role.</h2><p>Our established offshore operation is in Sri Lanka. We assess the role, experience, working hours and equipment before preparing an indicative staffing cost.</p><p>Australian customer support arrangements can be discussed where applicable. Your proposal confirms the commercial relationship, support scope and any equipment or infrastructure charges.</p><a class="text-link" href="/talent-locations/">Explore talent locations →</a></aside></section><CTASection/></Layout>
